BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-184208@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260518T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T190000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Love & Other Monsters" with Emily Frank
 lin
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 5 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184208
 \n\nBookmark the date for a captivating conversation exploring Love & Oth
 er Monsters by Emily Franklin—a richly imagined novel set against the ha
 unting backdrop of the “Year Without Summer.”\n\nIn 1816\, amid unrele
 nting storms on the shores of Lake Geneva\, a group of young literary icon
 s—including Mary and Percy Shelley and the infamous Lord Byron—gather 
 to create\, provoke\, and unravel. At the center of it all is Claire Clair
 mont: clever\, passionate\, and often overshadowed\, yet determined to car
 ve out her own identity in a world dominated by brilliance and ego. As rom
 ance\, rivalry\, and ambition collide\, Claire must navigate loyalty\, lon
 ging\, and the cost of living—and loving—on the edge of history.\n\nBl
 ending historical intrigue with emotional depth\, Love & Other Monsters e
 xplores the origins of legendary works like Frankenstein while giving voic
 e to the woman too often left out of the story.\n\nJoin us for an engaging
  discussion moderated by author Kerri Maher as we delve into this atmosphe
 ric novel and its themes of creativity\, fame\, and the monsters we make�
 �both real and imagined.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for 
 members only. Light refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184208
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
