BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-184947@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260521T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T183000
SUMMARY:Rethinking Women's Health: The Head & The Heart
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only
 \nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184947\n\n5:00PM Rece
 ption\, 5:30PM Discussion \nThe third installment in our Women’s Health
  Series explores the powerful and often underexamined connection between c
 ardiovascular and brain health—two systems deeply intertwined in shaping
  how we live\, age\, and thrive\n\nThis thoughtfully curated conversation 
 brings together two leading physicians whose work reflects both the scienc
 e and the human experience of health. Dr. Ami Bhatt—Chief Innovation Off
 icer at the American College of Cardiology and Chair of the FDA Digital He
 alth Advisory Committee—will explore the “heart” of the conversation
 \, offering insight into cardiovascular health\, innovation\, and the evol
 ving tools shaping prevention and care.\n\nComplementing this perspective\
 , Dr. Julia Loewenthal—Assistant Professor of Medicine at Harvard Medica
 l School and a board-certified internist and geriatrician—will guide the
  “head” of the discussion\, focusing on brain health\, aging\, and the
  ways cognitive conditions such as dementia uniquely impact women.\n\nDesi
 gned to inform and empower\, this program invites a more expansive underst
 anding of women’s health—one that recognizes the deep interconnection 
 between heart\, mind\, and longevity.\n\n*This event is complimentary and 
 reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites will be served\, and 
 beverages will be available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184947
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
