UID:quin-event-187622@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260610T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Checkmate" with Ben Mezrich
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 80 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1876
 22\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into the high-stakes wo
 rld of Checkmate with bestselling author Ben Mezrich—an electrifying tru
 e story that unravels the biggest scandal in modern chess.\n\nIn September
  2022\, the chess world was shaken when nineteen-year-old American prodigy
  Hans Niemann defeated reigning world champion Magnus Carlsen in a stunnin
 g upset. Days later\, Carlsen accused Niemann of cheating—an allegation 
 that ignited a global firestorm\, drawing in Chess.com\, the media\, and a
  rapidly expanding digital audience. What followed was a dramatic collisio
 n of reputation\, rivalry\, and power.\n\nBut Checkmate is about far more 
 than controversy. It’s a portrait of ambition at its sharpest edge—a y
 oung player willing to risk everything to rise\, and a legendary figure de
 termined to defend his legacy. Set against the backdrop of a centuries-old
  game transformed by streaming\, sponsorships\, and Silicon Valley influen
 ce\, Mezrich brings readers inside a world that is as cutthroat as it is c
 erebral.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Li
 ght bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
