LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 80 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1867
 25\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Performance\nWit & Word offers an evening 
 where humor is written\, spoken\, and felt—bringing together a standout 
 group of writers for a live\, spoken-word style performance that celebrate
 s the craft of comedy on the page. Moving beyond stand-up\, the night unfo
 lds through essays\, satire\, and personal storytelling—sharp\, candid\,
  and unexpectedly moving.\n\nGuiding the evening is award-winning comedian
  and The Moth regular Bethany Van Delft\, whose distinctive voice and gr
 ounded storytelling bring warmth\, wit\, and a natural sense of connection
  to the stage.\n\nThe lineup features Tracy McArdle Brady\, Founder and Ch
 ief Humorist of Wit & Word\; Steve Almond\, New York Times bestselling a
 uthor\; Lisa Borders\, award-winning novelist and McSweeney’s contributo
 r\; Neil Martinez-Belkin\, New York Times bestselling co-author and form
 er music editor of XXL Magazine\; and Viktoria Shulevich\, humor writer p
 ublished in The New Yorker and McSweeney’s. Together\, they explore th
 e absurdities and revelations of modern adulting through humor that is as 
 insightful as it is entertaining.\n\n*This event is complimentary and rese
 rved for members only. Light refreshments will be served and beverages wil
 l be available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186725
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
